<Layout
	title="Garden Sun privacy policy — Peculiar Engineer"
	description="What the Garden Sun iPhone app stores on your phone, what leaves it, and how to delete it."
	kind="page"
	showDate={false}
>
	<p><strong>Effective 26 November 2026</strong></p>
	<p>
		This policy covers the Garden Sun app. This website's own cookies are covered by the site's
		consent banner.
	</p>

	<h2>Summary</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>No account, analytics, ads or tracking.</li>
		<li>The app has no server of its own.</li>
		<li>Your spots, beds and plant choices stay on your iPhone.</li>
		<li>A rounded location goes to NASA POWER to estimate typical sun hours.</li>
		<li>Plant look-up uses Apple's Visual Look Up.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What the app stores on your phone</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Your spots, beds and plant choices. They are deleted when you delete the app.</li>
		<li>Replies from NASA POWER, cached for 30 days.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		You can export a spot file with the share sheet. It holds the spot's exact coordinates and
		your notes. You choose where it goes.
	</p>

	<h2>What leaves your phone</h2>
	<h3>NASA POWER</h3>
	<p>
		The app uses your location on the phone to work out where the sun is. To estimate typical sun
		hours, it rounds the location to a 0.5° grid (within about 30&nbsp;km of the real spot) and
		sends that to NASA POWER (<code>power.larc.nasa.gov</code>). NASA's servers also see your
		phone's internet (IP) address, as any website does. The reply is cached on your phone for
		30 days. See <a href="https://www.nasa.gov/privacy/">NASA's privacy policy</a>.
	</p>
	<h3>Apple Visual Look Up</h3>
	<p>
		Plant look-up uses Apple's Visual Look Up.
		<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a> covers what it
		processes. The app uploads no photos itself.
	</p>
	<p>
		Garden Sun shares data with these two services only, and only what is described here; each
		handles it under its own privacy policy, linked above, which gives it the same protection this
		policy describes.
	</p>
	<h3>Spot files you export</h3>
	<p>A spot file goes only where you choose to send or save it.</p>

	<h2>Camera, location and photos</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Location:</strong> used to work out where the sun is and, rounded as described
			above, to estimate typical sun hours.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Camera:</strong> used for the live Sun view and to photograph a plant.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Photos:</strong> you pick a photo with the system picker. The app sees only the
			photo you choose.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		You can turn location and camera access off at any time in iOS
		<strong>Settings → Garden Sun</strong>.
	</p>

	<h2>Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
	<p>
		Spots, beds and plant choices stay on your iPhone until you delete them with the app. To
		delete everything the app keeps, delete the app. A spot file you exported stays where you put
		it, so delete that copy there. Cached NASA POWER replies are kept on your phone for 30 days.
	</p>

	<h2>Children</h2>
	<p>
		Garden Sun is not directed at children under 13. It collects nothing that identifies anyone.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new effective date.</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about privacy or your data:
